UNIT tree_sha
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 e12613dad5808632c7fe28510214c96c79e264473e10d7833fc2a007d5805be8
SIG tree_sha(files: Record<string, string>): string
NOTE named export tree_sha
ABI map[text, text] = a plain object with own enumerable string keys (path) and string values (text); text = string
  (UTF-16). The result is a string of 64 lowercase hex characters. A throw (R2) is a thrown Error; the message is not
  graded. The artifact is an ES module exporting tree_sha; it may import node:crypto and nothing else. It never touches
  the file system: the map IS the tree.
MECHANISM SHA-256 (R4, R6, R7) = createHash('sha256').update(text, 'utf8').digest('hex') from node:crypto. NAMES (R1, R3) =
  path.split('/'). Validate every key (R1, R2) before hashing anything. The sort (R5) = Array.prototype.sort with no
  comparator, on the lines or on the paths — the host's default comparison IS UTF-16 code-unit order; never localeCompare,
  never Intl.Collator. The R2 message's path = JSON.stringify(path).
DEPENDS-ON none
PROVENANCE rederive@b15b56613f9d cli/tree-sha.mjs + selfhost/seams/tree_sha.mjs. Language file cut 2026-10-26 with the
  primary, before any blind re-emission; round 2 re-cut.
